From f8d725f8cb0a3e0b673208c25bed9a23336ac6c4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GrgaPalcic <26028466+GrgaPalcic@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 18:21:26 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] glm cuda: a cold pass seats in its held prefix's part; a
 cross-part keep evicts idle branches instead of refusing

Under TF_GLM_KV_SHARD with TF_KV_SHARE, a cold pass with nothing to resume was seated in the part with fewer live
streams. When the tree held its prefix (a system block, earlier turns) in the other part with other branches below,
every keep was refused (kv_shard_keeps_refused_total), so nothing was kept and every later turn ran cold again:
a 335K-token conversation re-prefilled for ~207 s each turn (a second two-Spark pair running this stack, 2026-11-11).

- The Prompts hooks gain an optional `first` (the first page the store holds of a prompt); cuda_share.prefixHome
  turns it into a part, and a cold pass with nothing adopted takes that part as its seat hint (the parts still
  choose when it lacks room), as a skipped resume already does.
- Store.keep: when the path would span the parts and the chain is not alone, the idle leaves under the chain go one
  at a time (Tree.evictUnder), then the chain is replaced whole as before. A refusal is left only when a live
  stream holds those leaves.
